---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Arhan Sibal";
const description =
  "Arhan Sibal is a strategy and operations professional with six years across ZS, BCG, Bain, Amazon, and Angel One, an MBA from Michigan Ross, and hands-on depth in analytics and AI.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>I turn messy business problems into systems that scale.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I have spent six years doing that across ZS, BCG, Bain, Amazon, and
      Angel One, in strategy, operations, and product roles. MBA from Michigan
      Ross, computer science from IIIT Delhi. The technical side never left.
      I still write my own SQL and Python, and I build AI tools when the off
      the shelf ones fall short.
    </p>
    <p class="hero-links">
      <a class="primary-link" href="/projects">See selected work</a>
      <a href="/writing">Read my writing</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strand" aria-labelledby="strategy-heading">
    <h2 id="strategy-heading">Strategy and operations</h2>
    <p>
      Most of my work starts with a vague question from leadership and ends
      with something a team can actually run every week. Market entry, cost
      models, operating metrics, the unglamorous middle of strategy where the
      slides have to survive contact with reality.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strand" aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
    <h2 id="analytics-heading">Analytics I can trace</h2>
    <p>
      I do the analysis myself rather than waiting in a queue for a data
      team. That keeps the loop between question and answer short, and it
      means every number in my recommendations is one I can defend line by
      line.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strand" aria-labelledby="ai-heading">
    <h2 id="ai-heading">AI I have actually built</h2>
    <p>
      I build with AI rather than just writing about it. The most recent
      example is
      <a
        href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/cgbimjanhgfjcopnpklcikkpcbgmjgoo"
        >J.A.N.E.</a
      >, a Chrome extension that helps job seekers cut through postings, pick
      the right resume, and draft outreach that sounds like them. More of this
      lives on the <a href="/projects">projects page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="close">
    <p>
      If something here is relevant to what you are working on, the fastest
      way to reach me is
      <a href="mailto:arhansibal10@gmail.com">arhansibal10@gmail.com</a>. The
      formal version of all this is on my <a href="/resume">resume</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5.5vw, 2.7rem);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .primary-link {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .primary-link:hover {
    background: #174734;
  }

  .strand {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .strand h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .strand p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .close {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .close p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
